{"title":"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A deck of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d98ffe996c0f0d3b82b284cba2113439fefea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> cards is given. A positive integer is written on each card. The deck has the property that the arithmetic mean of the numbers on each pair of cards is also the geometric mean of the numbers on some collection of one or more cards. \n</p><p>For which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> does it follow that the numbers on the cards are all equal?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Claim&#160;: For all n &gt; 1, all numbers must be equal<br />\nContradiction: Let us assume this is not true and for a certain n, there are k distinct positive integers which can be written in ascending order as follows&#160;: \n</p><p>z<sub>k</sub> &gt; z<sub>k-1</sub> &gt; z<sub>k-2</sub> &gt; … &gt; z<sub>1</sub>\n</p><p>Since z<sub>k</sub> is the largest of the numbers, it has to be greater than 1. This implies that there will be a prime p<sub>1</sub> that divides z<sub>k</sub>. \n</p><p>Now we know that the arithmetic mean of z<sub>k</sub> and z<sub>k-1</sub> is more than z<sub>k-1</sub>, thus the geometric mean which it is equivalent to must include the term z<sub>k</sub>. Since we know the arithmetic mean is a rational number, this means the root of the products of the n numbers of the geometric mean must be positive, and this will also divide p. \n</p><p>We can use similar argument for the sum of z<sub>k-1</sub> and z<sub>k-2</sub> will be greater than z<sub>k-2</sub> and thus the geometric mean is once again divisible by p. We can repeat this all the way to z<sub>1</sub>, which would mean that by dividing each term by p, we can reach another set of n cards which fulfil the conditions. We can keep applying this until z<sub>k</sub>. However this is a contradiction. \n</p><p>Thus, for all n &gt; 1, all the terms on the card will be equal. \n</p><p>QED\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution\">Video solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dTqwOoSfaAA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dTqwOoSfaAA</a> [video covers all day 2 problems]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO\" title=\"2020 IMO\">2020 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018013049\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 48/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 349/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.753      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.753      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:19752:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018013049 and revision id 257437. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}